.SH "NAME"
pcre2_substring_list_free \- free list of extracted substrings
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

void\fP \f(CBpcre2_substring_list_free\fP\f(CR(PCRE2_UCHAR **\fP\f(CIlist\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This is a convenience function for freeing the store obtained by a previous
call to \f(CBpcre2_substring_list_get()\fP. Its only argument is a pointer to
the list of string pointers. If the argument is \f(CBNULL\fP, the function returns
immediately, without doing anything.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.